<title>GERMANY: Holzmann - broke even in 96, plans job cuts.</title>
<headline>Holzmann - broke even in 96, plans job cuts.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philipp Holzmann AG, Germany's largest construction group, on Friday reported a break-even result for 1996 which took account of one billion marks ($610.7 million) in costs resulting from writedowns on share stakes, operating losses and provisions.</p>
<p>The group announced in a mandatory statement that it would continue to cut costs in 1997 and planned to reduce its workforce in Germany by 10 percent.</p>
<p>The group also said its construction output in 1996 was just under 14 billion marks, down from 14.1 billion marks in 1995.</p>
<p>Incoming orders totalled just under 16 billion marks, up from 15.6 billion marks, and orders in hand totalled more than 15 billion marks, up from 13.6 billion marks, Holzmann said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.637 German Marks)</p>
